there are actually two methods to solve z test and t test :

Method 1: Critical value method (uses the t-table)
Choose α (e.g., 0.05).
Calculate degrees of freedom (df).
Use α and df to find the critical t-value from the t-table.
Calculate the t-score (test statistic) using the formula.
Compare:
If ∣t∣> critical t → Reject H0.

Otherwise → Fail to reject H0

Why use α and df?

α tells you how much error you're willing to accept.
df changes the shape of the t-distribution, so the critical value depends on it.
Method 2: P-value method
Calculate the t-score.
Find the p-value corresponding to that t-score.
Compare:
If p ≤ α → Reject H0
	
